<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0;net11.0</TargetFrameworks>

    <!-- Enables trimming/AOT friendliness checks for consumers who publish trimmed. -->
    <IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Version, authors, licence, icon and Source Link come from src/Directory.Build.props. -->
  <PropertyGroup Label="Package metadata">
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>Idora.NET</PackageId>
    <Description>Idora generates prefixed, time-ordered entity identifiers such as usr_01k2f9v8ta7m3x0qbrn4dzeh5c. Each ID carries a per-entity prefix so you can tell what it identifies at a glance, followed by a lowercase ULID (default) or UUIDv7 so IDs sort by creation time and index well. Prefixes are registered once at startup, either fluently at DI setup or with an [EntityPrefix] attribute on the entity, eliminating magic strings and catching collisions at startup. IdoraId parses, validates and orders identifiers from any Idora package, and round-trips through JSON and model binding. Formerly published as UserFriendlyIds.</Description>
    <PackageTags>idora;id;identifier;ulid;uuid;uuidv7;guid;prefix;prefixed-id;sortable;time-ordered;dependency-injection;attribute;parse;validation</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
      1.1.0 - Reading and comparing identifiers.

      * IdoraId: a parsed identifier. Parse, TryParse and IsValid, strict, with an optional expected
        prefix; Prefix, Value, Format and Timestamp; equality, and a chronological natural order with
        operators; IsBefore/IsAfter, CompareTimestamp, IsSameMillisecond, IsCreatedBefore/After and
        HasPrefix. IParsable, ISpanParsable, ISpanFormattable and IUtf8SpanFormattable, and an
        implicit conversion to string.
      * IdoraId.LowerBound and UpperBound: the range of identifiers minted for one prefix during a
        span of time, for querying a key column by creation time with two string comparisons.
      * InvalidIdException and InvalidIdReason, raised when parsing fails.
      * IsIdFor, ParseIdFor and TryParseIdFor on IEntityPrefixRegistry: parse against the prefix
        registered for an entity type. GenerateId on IIdoraGenerator returns an IdoraId.
      * IdoraId serialises to JSON as a plain string, and has a TypeConverter, so it binds from routes,
        query strings and configuration with no setup.
      * New companion packages: Idora.NET.EntityFrameworkCore and Idora.NET.AspNetCore.
      * Targets net11.0 as well as net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0.

      Purely additive; nothing existing changes behaviour.

      1.0.0 - UserFriendlyIds is now Idora.NET.

      This is the UserFriendlyIds 1.1.0 feature set under a new name, as part of the Idora family of
      identically behaving packages for .NET, JavaScript/TypeScript, Java, Go and Rust. Identifiers
      are byte-for-byte the same format, so existing stored IDs remain valid.

      Breaking renames, all mechanical:

      * Package: UserFriendlyIds -> Idora.NET. Namespace and assembly: UserFriendlyIds -> Idora.
      * services.AddUserFriendlyIds(...) -> services.AddIdora(...).
      * IUserFriendlyIdGenerator -> IIdoraGenerator; UserFriendlyIdGenerator -> IdoraGenerator.
      * UserFriendlyIdOptions -> IdoraOptions; UserFriendlyIdsException -> IdoraException.

      Everything else - EntityPrefixAttribute, IEntityPrefixRegistry, IdGenerationStrategy and the
      other exception types - keeps its name and behaviour.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Idora.Tests" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Idora.Benchmarks" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
